NC Digital provides local SEO services for businesses across South Wales — helping you rank higher on Google, appear in local map results, and attract more customers from your area. We're based in Merthyr Tydfil and work with businesses across the entire South Wales region.

## Why local SEO matters for South Wales businesses

South Wales is a competitive market. Whether you're a plumber in Cardiff, a beauty salon in Swansea, or a builder in the Valleys — your customers are searching for your services on Google before they pick up the phone.

If your business isn't showing up, a competitor is getting that call instead.

Local SEO is what changes that. It's the process of making your business visible in Google Search and Google Maps when people in your area search for what you offer. Done properly, it's one of the most cost-effective ways a small business can generate consistent, high-quality leads — without paying for ads every month.

## What local SEO looks like in practice

Good local SEO isn't one thing — it's a combination of several signals working together:

**Google Business Profile** — Your GBP listing is what drives map visibility. A fully optimised profile with accurate details, good photos, regular posts, and strong reviews significantly outperforms a bare-bones listing.

**On-page SEO** — Your website needs to clearly signal what you do, where you do it, and who you do it for. That means proper page titles, relevant content, location signals, and internal linking.

**Local citations** — Consistent business name, address, and phone number across directories (Google, Bing, Yell, Checkatrade, and others) builds trust with search engines.

**Content** — Pages that answer the specific questions your customers are searching for — not just service pages, but useful, location-relevant content that earns rankings over time.

**Reviews** — Google uses review quantity, recency, and quality as a local ranking factor. We help clients build a steady stream of genuine reviews.

## What our SEO service includes each month

Every client gets a structured monthly service — not a vague "we'll do some SEO" package, but a specific set of actions each month focused on improving your rankings and generating more enquiries.

**Month 1 — Foundations**

- Full SEO audit (technical, on-page, and local)
- Keyword research tailored to your business, location, and target customers
- Google Business Profile setup or full optimisation
- On-page improvements to your most important pages (titles, headings, content, internal links)
- Local citation audit — checking your business details are consistent across directories

**Ongoing monthly work**

- New or improved content targeting the search terms your customers actually use
- Citation building across relevant UK and local directories
- Google Business Profile updates — posts, Q&A, image uploads, review monitoring
- Technical checks — crawl errors, broken links, page speed issues
- Monthly reporting in plain English — rankings, traffic, leads

## What results can you expect?

SEO is not instant — anyone promising page-one rankings in a few weeks is not being honest with you. Here's a realistic timeline:

- **Weeks 1–4**: Technical fixes, GBP improvements, and on-page changes go live
- **Months 2–3**: Google recognises the improvements; rankings for lower-competition terms start to move
- **Months 4–6**: Meaningful ranking improvements on target keywords; more impressions, clicks, and enquiries
- **6+ months**: Compounding results — rankings become more stable and harder for competitors to displace

Most clients see their first meaningful ranking improvements within 8–12 weeks. Enquiry increases typically follow within 3–5 months.

