## Frequently asked questions

**How long does local SEO take?**

Meaningful results typically appear within 3–6 months, though Google Business Profile improvements often show within 4–8 weeks. The speed depends on your competition, your starting position, and how much work is needed.

**Is SEO worth it for a small business in South Wales?**

Yes — especially for service businesses. When someone searches "roofer in Bridgend" or "accountant in Cardiff", they're actively looking to hire. Ranking for those terms puts you directly in front of people ready to spend. The ROI on local SEO is typically much stronger than paid ads for businesses with an established service.

**Do I need a Google Business Profile?**

Yes, for map visibility it's essential. We set it up and fully optimise it as part of the onboarding if you don't have one — or improve it if you do.

**What if I already have SEO being done?**

We offer a free audit so you can see exactly where you currently stand. If another agency is doing good work, we'll tell you. If there are gaps or problems, we'll show you what we'd do differently.

**Can you help a brand new business with no online presence?**

Absolutely. We've helped businesses start from scratch — building the website, setting up GBP, and running SEO from day one. Starting early gives you a head start on competitors who wait until later.

**Where are you based?**

[Merthyr Tydfil](/web-design-merthyr-tydfil/), South Wales — working with businesses across the region and beyond.

